 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? The easiest way is to measure your inseam, that's your leg length from crotch to the ground. Then add about ten centimeters. With your feet flat on the ground, there should be a slight bend in your knee. Too much straightness can feel uncomfortable after a while. Take your time. With your feet flat on ground, there should be a slight bend in your knee. Then add some spacers in the lower bracket. Most people need about half centimeter of room. Mostly. Lower the seat until the edge of the pedal is just about touching the ground.",
